86045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4}r^{2} \\left(r \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} + 12 r \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)\\,dr\\,d\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519836} :answer-field/id #uuid "492082b6-d4d5-536e-96d1-e4105c4455f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87c025ce-7c7a-5364-86fe-6c2155437fe3" :question/problem "![](images/44/44c489cbdf4665cca7fc7b8a331f5ccf4d72f8d15577f58c45497c58d5817bf3.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral\n\n$$\n\\oint_C(x y^{2} + 4 y^{3} - y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\,dx+(4 x^{3} + 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\,dy\\,?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\oint_C P\\,dx+Q\\,dy=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,dA.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](images/c4/c4cf3906e5af81f6cb071bae5b594861351987934fe6d51443c09e17982b2204.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=x y^{2} + 4 y^{3} - y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $Q(x,y)=4 x^{3} + 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=2 x y + 12 y^{2} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)},\\qquad\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}=12 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\oint_C(x y^{2} + 4 y^{3} - y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\,dx+(4 x^{3} + 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\,dy&=\\iint_D(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y})\\,dA\\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(12 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}-\\left(2 x y + 12 y^{2} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,dA\\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(12 x^{2} + 2 x y - 12 y^{2} + 2 y\\right)\\,dA.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\le r\\le 4,\\ 0\\le\\theta\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,dA=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D\\left(12 x^{2} + 2 x y - 12 y^{2} + 2 y\\right)\\,dA&=\\iint_\\Delta\\left(- 12 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)r\\,dr\\,d\\theta\\\\&=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4}r^{2} \\left(r \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} + 12 r \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b5e35f-78cc-50f2-aaa7-c2505886c068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4}-1\\,dr\\,d\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519773} {:answer/id #uuid "1e0a32b4-436c-52b0-8fcd-a18894aa9935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4}r\\,dr\\,d\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519780} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdc303e-a1be-599a-9867-656643cf200d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{4}- r\\,dr\\,d\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519801} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2ad259-18a1-56c3-a654-80f395f4a9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :